# What is not committed.
#
# The companion file is .dockerignore, which answers a different question -- what
# the image needs in its build context -- so the two lists differ on purpose:
#
#   example-dataset/, example-analysis/, tools/, README.md, CHANGELOG.md
#                      committed here, left out of the image: example data to
#                      mount rather than to bake in, the static checks for
#                      whoever edits a clone, and documentation
#   shiny-server/config.R, build-and-push.sh, and the leftovers below
#                      in neither

# macOS and editor leftovers
.DS_Store
._*

# R and Python working files. Rplots.pdf is what R opens when something plots
# with no graphics device, which is every headless Rscript run against the app.
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
Rplots.pdf
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The deployer's own configuration. It carries absolute local paths and the
# location of datasets that are not public, so it is the one file here that must
# never be published. config.example.R is what ships in its place, and
# R/09_config.R explains what CRAVE does when config.R is absent.
/shiny-server/config.R

# Publishing the image is done from the development tree, not from a clone.
/build-and-push.sh

# Built images and anything saved beside them.
/images/
*.tar.gz

# Runtime state a dataset accumulates: the metadata cache CRAVE writes beside a
# dataset, and everything the Submit tab keeps (workbooks, counts matrices,
# result tables, job logs). Both appear inside example-dataset/data/ the first
# time the app is run against it, and neither is part of the dataset.
.crave-cache/
.crave-submit/
